/** @mainpage

This suite exercises tsf-sctp - opening an SCTP (RFC 9260) association
to a peer from the Test Agent it runs on, over the Linux lksctp sockets
API:

- @ref sctp-probe - connect to a peer, read the negotiated association
  (state, inbound/outbound stream counts, path MTU, multihoming address
  lists), and assert it is established.

SCTP is the transport under the telecom signalling stacks (SIGTRAN/M3UA,
Diameter, S1AP/NGAP) and WebRTC data channels - none of which TE's
TCP/UDP stack can carry. The association runs in the agent's RPC server
and is read-only. The peer is supplied via TSF_SCTP_HOST / TSF_SCTP_PORT;
with none configured the suite skips cleanly, so a bare run is green.

*/
